---
// The home page uses BaseLayout rather than ContentLayout, because
// ContentLayout's only header is a full-bleed photo with the title laid over
// it. That spent a whole screen on a title and a picture and pushed the
// course's argument below the fold. CourseHeader goes into the hero slot
// instead, so the band is still edge to edge but carries the record, the
// teaching pattern and two ways in.
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import BaseLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CourseHeader from "../components/CourseHeader.astro";
import HoldPattern from "../components/HoldPattern.astro";
import Thesis from "../components/Thesis.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
import "../styles/wait.css";
---

<BaseLayout title={courseMeta.title} description={courseMeta.description} {...siteConfig}>
  <CourseHeader slot="hero" />

  <HoldPattern />

  <Thesis />

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    You log a week of your own waits and find out that the clock and the
    feeling disagree. You take one shipped wait apart and work out which of
    the things it measures, shows and claims is actually holding it up. Then
    you redesign a wait you are not allowed to make shorter, and say out loud
    who your redesign is managing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in this course asks you to make anything faster. The duration
    stays where it is in every exercise, which leaves you the techniques and
    the argument about who they are pointed at.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Second year and above, in interaction design, service design or software.
    You need to be able to build or prototype an interface well enough that
    somebody else can use it, and to sit with an argument that does not
    resolve. No statistics background is assumed, although you will read
    papers that have some in them.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you want a course on performance optimisation, this is the wrong one.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>What each week's lecture argues, and the slides where there are any.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</BaseLayout>
